<TextPage
	title="Privacy — Hookd"
	description="What this site collects: essentially nothing. No accounts, no cookies, no tracking, no newsletter."
	heading="Privacy"
	standfirst="Short, because the site does very little. It is a set of static pages with no accounts, no forms and no tracking."
	updated="Last updated 19 August 2026"
>
	<h2>What is collected</h2>

	<p>
		Nothing that identifies you. There are no accounts, no comment section, no contact form and
		no newsletter signup. The site sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and stores nothing in your
		browser.
	</p>

	<h2>Hosting logs</h2>

	<p>
		The site is served as static files by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes
		technical request data — IP address, timestamp, the page requested, your browser's
		user-agent — in order to deliver the page and to protect against abuse. I do not have
		access to those logs as an identifiable record of individual visitors, and I do not combine
		them with anything else.
	</p>

	<h2>Fonts</h2>

	<p>
		Typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts, which means your browser makes a request to Google's
		servers and Google receives your IP address as part of that request. This is worth knowing
		because it is the one third party the site currently contacts.
	</p>

	<div class="placeholder">
		<strong>Open question</strong>
		Under GDPR, loading fonts from Google has been found problematic in some EU decisions.
		Self-hosting the font files would remove this entirely and is a small change. Worth doing
		before launch — noted in TODO.md.
	</div>

	<h2>Analytics</h2>

	<p>
		There are currently none. If analytics are added, it will be Cloudflare Web Analytics,
		which is cookieless and does not fingerprint or track individuals across sites — and this
		page will be updated to say so.
	</p>

	<h2>Links out</h2>

	<p>
		Links to Ravelry, Instagram, Pinterest, YouTube and yarn suppliers lead to sites with their
		own privacy policies. This one does not cover them.
	</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>

	<p>
		Under the GDPR you have the right to access, correct and erase personal data held about
		you, and to complain to a supervisory authority. Since this site holds no personal data
		about you, there is in practice nothing to access or erase — but if you believe otherwise,
		get in touch and I will look into it.
	</p>

